{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-87821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $3(2-5x)^{9}+5\\le 8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the ninth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2-5x)^{9}+5 & \\le 8 \\\\ 3(2-5x)^{9} & \\le 3 \\\\ (2-5x)^{9} & \\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the ninth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[9]{(2-5x)^{9}} & \\le \\sqrt[9]{1} \\\\ 2-5x & \\le 1 \\\\ -5x & \\le -1 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-87821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "x\\ge -\\frac{8}{3}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "x\\le -\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(x-6)^{3}+5\\le 0.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{3}+5 & \\le 0 \\\\ (x-6)^{3} & \\le -5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the third root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-6)^{3}} & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5} \\\\ x-6 & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5} \\\\ x & \\le \\sqrt[3]{-5}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278048" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-5^{\\frac{1}{3}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(x+5)^{7}-1\\ge 8.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the seventh-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)^{7}-1 & \\ge 8 \\\\ (x+5)^{7} & \\ge 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the seventh root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{(x+5)^{7}} & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{9} \\\\ x+5 & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{9} \\\\ x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{9}-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278051" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9^{\\frac{1}{7}}-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(3-x)^{7}-8\\ge 5.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the seventh-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-x)^{7}-8 & \\ge 5 \\\\ (3-x)^{7} & \\ge 13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the seventh root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{(3-x)^{7}} & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13} \\\\ 3-x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13} \\\\ -x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13}-3 \\\\ x & \\le -\\sqrt[7]{13}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\le"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278121" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-13^{\\frac{1}{7}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $(5-2x)^{3}-60\\ge 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-2x)^{3}-60 & \\ge 4 \\\\ (5-2x)^{3} & \\ge 64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(5-2x)^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{64} \\\\ 5-2x & \\ge 4 \\\\ -2x & \\ge -1 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-87448" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87448" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge 1"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87448" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\le \\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $4(1-x)^{6}-1>7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(1-x)^{6}-1 & >7 \\\\ 4(1-x)^{6} & >8 \\\\ (1-x)^{6} & >2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the sixth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{(1-x)^{6}} & >\\sqrt[6]{2} \\\\ |1-x| & >\\sqrt[6]{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n1-x<-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,1-x>\\sqrt[6]{2}\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-x & <-\\sqrt[6]{2} &  &  & 1-x & >\\sqrt[6]{2} \\\\ -x & <-\\sqrt[6]{2}-1 &  &  & -x & >\\sqrt[6]{2}-1 \\\\ x & >1+\\sqrt[6]{2} &  &  & x & <1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is\n\n$$\nx<1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-116221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<-1-\\sqrt[6]{2}"] ["math" "x<0"] ["math" "x<1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}"] ["math" "x>-2"] ["math" "x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x<1-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>1+\\sqrt[6]{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $-4(5-x)^{6}+147>-109.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(5-x)^{6}+147 & >-109 \\\\ -4(5-x)^{6} & >-256 \\\\ (5-x)^{6} & <64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the inequality when we divided both sides by $-4.$\n\nNow, we take the sixth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{(5-x)^{6}} & <\\sqrt[6]{64} \\\\ |5-x| & <2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-2<5-x<2\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2<5-x & <2 \\\\ -7<-x & <-3 \\\\ 7>x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the lower number is on the left:\n\n$$\n3<x<7\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278143" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $(5-x)^{2}+4\\le 6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quadratic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-x)^{2}+4 & \\le 6 \\\\ (5-x)^{2} & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the square root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(5-x)^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{2} \\\\ |5-x| & \\le \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{2}\\le 5-x\\le \\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2}\\le 5-x & \\le \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}-5\\le -x & \\le \\sqrt{2}-5 \\\\ 5+\\sqrt{2}\\ge x & \\ge 5-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the lower number is on the left:\n\n$$\n5-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 5+\\sqrt{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-87918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "5-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 5+\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "x\\ge 5-\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "x\\le \\sqrt{2}+5"] ["text" "$x\\le -5-\\sqrt{2}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 5-\\sqrt{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 5+\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(4-x)^{2}-10\\ge 7.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quadratic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4-x)^{2}-10 & \\ge 7 \\\\ (4-x)^{2} & \\ge 17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the square root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{17} \\\\ |4-x| & \\ge \\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n4-x\\le -\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{or}\\,4-x\\ge \\sqrt{17}\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-x & \\le -\\sqrt{17} &  &  & 4-x & \\ge \\sqrt{17} \\\\ -x & \\le -\\sqrt{17}-4 &  &  & -x & \\ge \\sqrt{17}-4 \\\\ x & \\ge 4+\\sqrt{17} &  &  & x & \\le 4-\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\le 4-\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge 4+\\sqrt{17}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4-\\sqrt{17}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-278138" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4+\\sqrt{17}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2(x+4)^{4}+6<18.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)^{4}+6 & <18 \\\\ 2(x+4)^{4} & <12 \\\\ (x+4)^{4} & <6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(x+4)^{4}} & <\\sqrt[4]{6} \\\\ |x+4| & <\\sqrt[4]{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt[4]{6}<x+4<\\sqrt[4]{6}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[4]{6}<x+4 & <\\sqrt[4]{6} \\\\ -\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x & <\\sqrt[4]{6}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-116224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x<\\sqrt[4]{6}-4"] ["math" "x<\\sqrt[4]{6}+3"] ["math" "x<\\sqrt[4]{6}-4"] ["math" "x>\\sqrt[4]{6}+1"] ["text" "$x<-\\sqrt[4]{6}-2\\,$ or $\\,x>\\sqrt[4]{6}-2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116224" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x<\\sqrt[4]{6}-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve $4(2-x)^{8}+3\\ge -9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the eighth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2-x)^{8}+3 & \\ge -9 \\\\ 4(2-x)^{8} & \\ge -12 \\\\ (2-x)^{8} & \\ge -3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(2-x)^{8}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-87840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "valu