 inequality is all real numbers." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-87834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<-3"] ["math" "x>1"] ["text" "$x<-1$ or $x>3$"] ["text" "All real numbers"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-87834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "All real numbers"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve $2(2-5x)^{8}+7<3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the eighth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2-5x)^{8}+7 & <3 \\\\ 2(2-5x)^{8} & <-4 \\\\ (2-5x)^{8} & <-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(2-5x)^{8}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-116241" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116241" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<0"] ["math" "x>0"] ["math" "x>\\sqrt[8]{2}"] ["text" "All real numbers"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116241" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve $(4x-5)^{4}+25\\le 9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quartic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4x-5)^{4}+25 & \\le 9 \\\\ (4x-5)^{4} & \\le -16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(4x-5)^{4}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(4)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ee53dbb24f84fafeb03a70462a6c3241b78729c375ea615eec9718c57265b8c2"} {"question" "q-116229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -4"] ["math" "x\\ge 0"] ["math" "x\\le 4"] ["text" "All real numbers"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "q-116229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/state.json" "file_sha256" "b12ce344c449fe07539e1831a3343a1a8fb3066a4f73fe246d81828e96bc84a8"} {"question" "e-7651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2(x - 2)^3 - 5 \\gt      11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/example-7651.json" "file_sha256" "ba64be1d489bf5463455a839233ae704c4f5cdf8797a90c028a7a214bc821db6"} {"question" "e-7651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{3}-5 & >11 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{3} & >16 \\\\ (x-2)^{3} & >8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-2)^{3}} & >\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x-2 & >2 \\\\ x & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/example-7651.json" "file_sha256" "ba64be1d489bf5463455a839233ae704c4f5cdf8797a90c028a7a214bc821db6"} {"question" "e-7653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(5x + 2)^4}{9} - 3 \\gt 6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/example-7653.json" "file_sha256" "6d75c65f21dd554c0497742eb2ab3c8ffa0c442e93d66a9cda910c63b605e8ea"} {"question" "e-7653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9}-3 & >6 \\\\ \\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9} & >9 \\\\ (5x+2)^{4} & >81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(5x+2)^{4}} & >\\sqrt[4]{81} \\\\ |5x+2| & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n5x + 2 \\lt -3 \\qquad \\textrm{or} \\qquad 5x + 2 \\gt 3\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2 & <-3 &  &  & 5x+2 & >3 \\\\ 5x & <-5 &  &  & 5x & >1 \\\\ x & <-1 &  &  & x & >\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\lt -1 \\quad \\textrm{or} \\quad x \\gt \\dfrac{1}{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/example-7653.json" "file_sha256" "6d75c65f21dd554c0497742eb2ab3c8ffa0c442e93d66a9cda910c63b605e8ea"} {"question" "e-7652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/example-7652.json" "file_sha256" "e2bc6660c0e290a4df729f871f45590d0f25080c7d8e961089179b18a9996245"} {"question" "e-7652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)^{6}+5 & \\ge -4 \\\\ (5x-1)^{6} & \\ge -9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981470/example-7652.json" "file_sha256" "e2bc6660c0e290a4df729f871f45590d0f25080c7d8e961089179b18a9996245"}] "usage" {"q-87448" [] "e-7653" [] "e-7651" [] "e-7652" []} "basis" 888 "retractions" [[17592186157827 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $(5 - 2x)^{3} - 60 \\ge 4$."] [17592186157062 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2(x - 2)^3 - 5 \\gt 11$."] [17592186157062 :question/worked-solution "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2(x - 2)^{3} - 5 & > 11 \\\\ 2(x - 2)^{3} & > 16 \\\\ (x - 2)^{3} & > 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[3]{(x - 2)^{3}} & > \\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x - 2 & > 2 \\\\ x & > 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186157064 :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(5x + 2)^4}{9} - 3 \\gt 6$."] [17592186157064 :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n$\\begin{bmatrix}((5x + 2)^{4})/(9) - 3 & > 6 \\\\ ((5x + 2)^{4})/(9) & > 9 \\\\ (5x + 2)^{4} & > 81\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n$\\sqrt[4]{(5x + 2)^{4}} \\mid > \\sqrt[4]{81}; \\mid 5x + 2 \\mid \\mid > 3$.\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n$5x + 2 \\lt -3 \\qquad \\textrm{or} \\qquad 5x + 2 \\gt 3$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5x + 2 & < - 3 & 5x + 2 & > 3 \\\\ 5x & < - 5 & 5x & > 1 \\\\ x & < - 1 & x & > \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\lt -1 \\quad \\textrm{or} \\quad x \\gt \\dfrac{1}{5}\n$$"] [17592186157063 :question/problem "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4$."] [17592186157063 :question/worked-solution "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(5x - 1)^{6} + 5 & \\ge - 4 \\\\ (5x - 1)^{6} & \\ge - 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186156215 17592186156216 17592186156217 17592186156218 17592186156219] "immutable_fields" [[17592186156214 :answer-field/correct] [17592186156214 :answer-field/id] [17592186156214 :answer-field/key] [17592186156214 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
